## 12. User Roles and Authorization

Support role-based access control.

Suggested application permission roles:

- Super Administrator
- HR Administrator
- Division Manager
- Employee

These are application access roles and are separate from employment job titles.

Super Administrator:
- Manage authorized system settings.
- Manage application access roles.
- Manage divisions and job-title configuration.
- Manage employees and HR records.
- Access organization-wide reporting when authorized.

HR Administrator:
- Create and update employee records.
- Manage employment documents and contracts.
- Review onboarding and document completeness.
- Generate authorized HR reports.

Division Manager:
- View employees assigned to their permitted division.
- Access approved employment information.
- Perform specifically authorized employee-management tasks.

Employee:
- View their own profile.
- View their own permitted employment records.
- Update approved personal fields.
- Upload permitted documents.
- View their own contract information when allowed.
- Track their own onboarding status.

Implement authorization in the backend or trusted server-side layer, not just by hiding buttons in the frontend.

An employee must never gain administrative privileges simply by changing a URL, editing browser state, or modifying a request.

Follow the organization's actual authorization policy when assigning final permissions.

